# Where hachiko alerts and whose reply it takes, both required: the bot is how everything
# it has to say goes out, so a channel missing here is an alert with nowhere to go, and
# answering the on-call session from Discord needs the account as well. Neither is a secret
# — a channel id is in the URL of every message in it and a user id is on Tim's own profile
# — so they are here rather than in 1Password, and the bot token that is a secret is a
# reference in hachiko.env.op beside the wrapper.
#
# channel: the private forum channel hachiko alerts to. Each incident gets a post in it,
#          tagged Open while it runs and Resolved and closed when it is over.
# user:    the one account a reply is taken from. Everything else in the thread is ignored,
#          the bot's own messages included, because a reply is an instruction to an agent
#          with authority over this Mac.
# updates: a plain text channel for the nightly update's summary of what moved, which is
#          not an incident and has nothing to answer. Optional: without it the summary
#          stays in hachiko's own log, and anything the update failed at is still an
#          incident in the forum above.
#
# Both are snowflakes: enable Developer Mode in Discord and copy the id.
#
# What else it needs: a Discord application with a bot, the Message Content intent turned
# on, invited to the server with permission to read messages, send them, send them in
# threads, create public threads, manage threads, add reactions and read message history —
# manage threads being what closes a post the bot did not open; an Open tag and a Resolved
# tag on the forum; a `bot token` field on the hachiko-discord item in the dev vault; and an
# `approval` one-time-password field on the same item, which is the second factor an action
# on the never list needs. README has the whole of it under hachiko.

